>> title: Flan
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: custard, caramel, milk, oven, make-ahead
>> counters: Taquería, Panadería
>> aka: flan napolitano, crème caramel, creme caramel, caramel custard
>> servings: 8
>> time: 6 hr
>> step.2: cook to an amber caramel
>> step.4: whisk in the milks
>> step.5: strain over the caramel
>> step.6: bake at 325°F in a water bath 55 min
>> step.7: chill 4 hr, then invert

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (165°C) and set a #9-in round cake pan{} inside a roasting pan.

Cook @granulated sugar{1%cup}(200 g), @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in a #saucepan{} to an amber caramel, then swirl it over the bottom of the cake pan.

Whisk @eggs{4%large}(200 g), @egg yolks{2%large}(37 g), @vanilla extract{2%tsp}(10 mL), @table salt{1/4%tsp} until smooth.

Whisk @sweetened condensed milk{14%oz}(one 396 g can), @evaporated milk{12%oz}(354 mL), @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) into @&(~1)eggs{}.

Pour @&(~1)custard{} through a fine sieve over @&(~3)caramel{}.

Bake @&(~1)flan{} in a water bath at 325°F for ~{55%min}, until the centre jiggles as one piece.

Chill @&(~1)flan{} for ~{4%hr}, then run a knife around the rim and invert onto a rimmed plate.
